nment:* Directly addresses Article 12(2)(b) (post-market monitoring). It transforms a regulatory burden into a research asset, which fits an R&D institution's goals.\n    *   *Resource Commitment:* Requires engineering effort to set up the \"shared analytics store\" and ingestion pipeline, but once established, it scales across prototypes.\n\n    *   The proposal is technically sound.\n    *   It leverages regulatory requirements to create research value (longitudinal datasets).\n    *   As a Dev Engineer, I prefer systems that automate data collection over manual auditing.\n    *   Potential friction: Ensuring the \"cross-team group\" doesn't slow down prototype deployment with excessive metric definitions. But overall, the infrastructure for logging is essential anyway for debugging and quality assurance.\n\n    *   Rationale: Building a standardized ingestion pipeline for operational logs is technically viable and converts a compliance requirement into a high-value longitudinal research asset without significantly hindering prototyping speed once the infrastructure is in place.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: 85 (Strongly positive, though some caution on potential overhead of per-system metric definition).",
