 to work.\n    *   Immutable storage and retrievability are standard requirements for enterprise-grade systems anyway.\n    *   While it adds some friction (the \"gate\"), it prevents the catastrophic failure of shipping a non-compliant high-risk system, which would require massive rework later.\n\n    *   Rationale: It transforms vague regulatory requirements into concrete technical specifications and acceptance tests without hindering the initial prototyping speed. Ensuring logging is handled before deployment avoids costly architectural refactors late in the lifecycle.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: 85 (It's a solid process improvement, though slightly bureaucratic).",
