* Article 12 requires high-risk systems to \"technically allow for the automatic recording of events.\" This proposal doesn't just build a logging tool; it integrates the *logic* and *analysis* of that logging into the scientific process, ensuring compliance is built-in by design rather than bolted on.\n\n    *   *Pros:* Synergistic approach (compliance + science), improves lab prestige/rigor, avoids \"double work\" where engineers log for compliance and researchers document for papers separately.\n    *   *Cons:* Might add friction to the research process; requires buy-in from a \"methodology committee.\" However, the cost is primarily administrative/cultural rather than financial.\n\n    *   Rationale: This proposal strategically converts a mandatory regulatory burden into a scientific asset, enhancing the lab's intellectual prestige while ensuring systematic compliance with Article 12. It optimizes resource allocation by merging compliance engineering with core research objectives.\n    *   Decision: Approve.\n    *   Promise: High (e.g., 85-90). It turns an obligation into a competitive advantage.",
