 vs. Ambition:* While it consumes resources, the risk of non-compliance for \"high-risk\" systems under the EU AI Act is an existential threat to funding and market access. A structured lifecycle is more efficient than frantic, last-minute documentation efforts before a regulatory audit.\n\n    *   The proposal is highly pragmatic. It leverages existing infrastructure (version control) and creates clear accountability (Project Lead). While it adds overhead, the cost of *not* having this in place for high-risk systems is far higher (potential fines, loss of market access). From a Lab Director's perspective, systematizing compliance reduces \"fire drills\" that disrupt scientific work.\n\n    *   Rationale: This proposal establishes a systematic approach to satisfy Recital 71 requirements using existing version-control infrastructure, reducing the risk of costly regulatory failures and disruptive last-minute audits. Although it introduces personnel overhead via Project Leads, this is a necessary investment to ensure our high-risk systems are commercially viable and legally compliant.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: 85 (It's highly promising because it transforms a chaotic regulatory requirement into a manageable process, though the per-project lead role might be tweaked for efficiency later).",
