ntific errors due to fragmented or inconsistent logging implementations.\n\n    *   Rationale: Centralizing compliance infrastructure minimizes the diversion of research talent from core scientific objectives and prevents \"compliance fatigue\" across multiple projects. It allows researchers to maintain focus on the knowledge frontier by automating the mundane requirements of Article 12.\n    *   Decision: Approve.\n    *   Promise: High (e.g., 85-90) because it's a practical win for research productivity.\n\n    *   Check constraints: Rationale first, then decision, then promise integer. Echo ID. No ranking against others.",
