ce during R&D suggests institutional maturity and reliability.\n\n    *   The proposal integrates compliance into the existing operational rhythm. This is highly efficient.\n    *   It forces Principal Investigators (PIs) to take ownership of the compliance checklist monthly.\n    *   By aligning with budget/progress reviews, it links funding/progress to regulatory adherence—a strong motivator in an R&D environment.\n    *   Risk: Is a one-page checklist sufficient? For *verification* that logging is implemented, yes; for the actual *technical implementation*, no (but this proposal isn't about building the logger, but about *verifying* it).\n\n    *   Rationale: Integrating compliance checks into existing milestones ensures continuous monitoring and accountability without creating bureaucratic friction that researchers would resist. It transforms regulatory adherence from a final hurdle into a project management standard.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: 85 (Highly effective for governance, though the actual \"checklist\" content will need rigorous design to ensure it meets Article 12's technical specifics).",
