ided. It mitigates the risk of non-compliance by making traceability a fundamental constraint rather than an optional feature. While it consumes resources (ML researchers, systems engineer), the payoff in terms of regulatory safety and institutional reputation is significant.\n\n    *   Rationale: This proposal shifts compliance from a reactive checklist to a systemic architectural requirement, directly addressing Article 12's mandate for automatic logging while minimizing the risk of retrospective failure. It protects the institution by ensuring all high-risk systems are compliant by design and enhances our market position as leaders in transparent, auditable AI.\n    *   Decision: approve\n    *   Promise: 95 (Very strong; addresses a core legal requirement with a robust engineering approach).",
