leverage.\n    *   However, Article 12 is a mandate for \"high-risk\" systems. If the lab's R&D output includes high-risk systems, they *must* implement this anyway. Building a reusable library (even if open-sourced) is more efficient than every project team reinventing the logging wheel.\n    *   The \"thought leadership\" and \"regulator goodwill\" are strategic assets that can protect funding or facilitate smoother audits in the future.\n    *   Compared to the cost of potential non-compliance fines under the EU AI Act, a small investment in a standardized tool is highly efficient.\n\n    *   *Rationale:* Building a reusable library prevents fragmented implementation across multiple internal projects and leverages regulatory compliance as a strategic asset for institutional prestige. The resource requirement is modest compared to the risk mitigation and efficiency gains of a standardized logging framework.\n    *   *Decision:* Approve.\n    *   *Promise:* High (85-90), because it turns a mandatory burden into a strategic advantage without excessive headcount.",
